<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khammao Vilay</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Phaya Khammao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khammao Vilay was a Lao official who served as prime minister of the Lao Issara government formed in Vientiane in October 1945 after the Japanese surrender. His cabinet, which included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souvanna-phouma">Souvanna Phouma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souphanouvong">Souphanouvong</a>, opposed the return of French rule but had little money or military force. When French troops retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> in 1946 he went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a> with the movement's government.</p></div>
